Package: betaem
Type: Package
Title: Expectation-Maximisation for Beta Mixture Models
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(person("Kevin", "Gori", email = "kcg25@cam.ac.uk", role = c("aut", "cre")))
Maintainer: Kevin Gori <kcg25@cam.ac.uk>
Description: Fits a mixture of Beta distributions to data in [0, 1] using the
    Expectation-Maximisation algorithm. The core EM loop, E-step (weight
    computation via log-sum-exp) and M-step (moment-matched parameter updates)
    are implemented in C++ via Rcpp and RcppArmadillo for maximum performance.
    An R-level wrapper preserves optional per-iteration plotting for
    diagnostic use.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
LazyData: true
Depends: R (>= 3.5.0)
Imports:
    Rcpp (>= 1.0.0),
    grid,
    gridBase,
    gridExtra
LinkingTo:
    Rcpp,
    RcppArmadillo
RoxygenNote: 7.2.0
